bout you and me.␀␀ˇˇWhat! There is no you and me.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇYeah, yeah there is. See,␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇfirst you rescued my notes from Mandy,␀␀␀␀ˇˇand then we fell in love, and you brought me flowers␀␀ˇˇand wrote me poetry, and showed this kinder,␀␀ˇˇsensitive side that soon␀␀ˇˇthe whole world is gonna know about.␀␀ˇˇWe're like doomed lovers.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇEnough! OK, I'll get your book back.␀␀ˇˇThen, we can kiss!␀␀␀␀ˇˇThe cold sores aren't contagious␀␀ˇˇonce they start to scab over!␀␀␀␀␀mP∫␀␀␀nP∫!␀␀␀oP∫1␀␀␀pP∫i␀␀␀qP∫Å␀␀␀rP∫≈␀␀␀sP∫ı␀␀␀tP∫5␀␀uP∫i␀␀ÔP∫Ö␀␀P∫µ␀␀ÒP∫›␀␀ÚP∫␀␀ÛP∫1␀␀ÙP∫=␀␀ıP∫m␀␀ˆP∫ë␀␀˜P∫±␀␀¯P∫›␀␀rQ∫␀␀sQ∫E␀␀tQ∫a␀␀uQ∫â␀␀vQ∫©␀␀wQ∫—␀␀xQ∫È␀␀yQ∫␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀4Õ´␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ ␀␀␀␀!␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀BD␀␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇSchool rules are quite clear on this subject. Quite clear.␀␀␀␀ˇˇNo alcohol on school grounds.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇYou're drunk.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇI can smell it on your breath.␀␀␀␀ˇˇI CAN SEE IT IN YOUR EYES.␀␀␀␀ˇˇI'm not drunk.␀␀␀␀ˇˇDrunk, in charge of children.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇWhat kind of monster drinks in front of children?␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇA parent?␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇA disgraceful one, yes!␀␀␀ˇˇYou've got a problem, haven't you?␀␀␀␀ˇˇI'm just under a lot of pressure.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇWell, I'm a kind and supportive colleague, Galloway,␀␀ˇˇand as such I think it is my duty to get you sacked.␀␀ˇˇDo whatever you want, Hattrick. You always do.␀␀␀␀ˇˇThe head will find out about this.␀␀␀␀ˇˇYou OK, sir?␀␀ˇˇAaah, Jimmy! No. I'm not OK.␀␀ˇˇI'm half drunk, and about to get fired. Fantastic!␀␀␀␀ˇˇI'm a washed up old drunk, and I'm only 34.␀␀␀ˇˇEnglish you see, is a difficult subject to teach.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇI've tried any number of things to dull the pain␀␀ˇˇ- yoga, meditation, needle point,␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇlooking at dubious sites on the internet.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇBut nothing dulls the pain like Scotch.␀␀␀ˇˇCome on Sir, put that away.␀␀␀ˇˇAre you mad? This is manna from the gods.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇGimme that.␀␀␀ˇˇLet's get rid of this before you get busted.␀␀ˇˇThat's very kind of you Jimmy.␀␀␀␀ˇˇMs. Philips is the only teacher␀␀␀ˇˇto know about my vice - take it to her␀␀␀␀ˇˇ- she will know what to do.␀␀␀”ÃY>␀␀␀‘ÃY>A␀␀␀’ÃY>e␀␀␀÷ÃY>y␀␀␀◊ÃY>ù␀␀␀ÿÃY>Ω␀␀␀ŸÃY>—␀␀␀⁄ÃY>ı␀␀␀€ÃY>-␀␀UÕY>=␀␀VÕY>Y␀␀WÕY>Å␀␀XÕY>©␀␀YÕY>·␀␀ZÕY>␀␀[ÕY>M␀␀\ÕY>u␀␀]ÕY>Ö␀␀^ÕY>•␀␀ÿÕY>›␀␀ŸÕY>␀␀⁄ÕY>E␀␀€ÕY>y␀␀‹ÕY>°␀␀›ÕY>—␀␀ﬁÕY>˝␀␀ﬂÕY>␀␀‡ÕY>M␀␀·ÕY>]␀␀[ŒY>ç␀␀\ŒY>±␀␀]ŒY>’␀␀^ŒY>␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀4Õ´␀␀␀␀␀␀␀\␀␀p␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀BD␀␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇThat kid?  Never seen him before.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇHe looks kinda dumb.␀␀ˇˇ"This is a warning Hopkins.  I'll let you off this time, but next time you're going to the principal's office."␀␀␀ˇˇGo to the Principal's office.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇYou're dead new kid, dead.␀␀␀␀ˇˇPrefect!␀␀ˇˇHey... you wanna play Grottos and Gremlins some time?␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇHello there ma'am.␀␀␀␀ˇˇGo to the Principal's office.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇRusell hates new kids.␀␀␀␀ˇˇHey check it out. A new boy.␀␀ˇˇWho cares?  Let's go tell Russell, we'll get a little party toge