trice.␀␀␀␀ˇˇ~t~ Exit School␀␀␀ˇˇCheck the math room.␀␀ˇˇ~t~ Exit␀␀ˇˇEnter the school through the rear window.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇLocked. Check the lockers by the staff room.␀␀ˇˇReturn the diary to Beatrice.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇLocked. Check the staff room.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇCheck the math room.␀␀ˇˇDid you like the part about you being like a Roman Emperor.␀␀␀ˇˇOh there you are... did you get it?␀␀␀\u˙␀␀␀Ä§q␀␀␀∆+1␀␀␀ïDØ]␀␀␀7√!i␀␀␀Ö!}␀␀␀Ü!Â␀␀Îù'Ω␀␀*44—␀␀Ïî°6È␀␀\M’7˝␀␀l§8␀␀lº¯C=␀␀f}IY␀␀Òì√Iç␀␀åXK≠␀␀a^N’␀␀Ç0WÈ␀␀ ùX˝␀␀nåUh␀␀]K*k!␀␀^K*kQ␀␀_K*kÅ␀␀`K*k•␀␀aK*k…␀␀>√Ên·␀␀îo!␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀4Õ´␀␀␀␀␀␀␀\␀␀¯␀␀?␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀BD␀␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇOf course of course... and normally I would never interfere.␀␀ˇˇYou'll see, he won't get away with it this time.␀␀ˇˇVery good.  Best be off to class then... and thanks.␀␀ˇˇI hope you are wrong, for the sake of Bullworth.␀␀ˇˇHitting the sauce, are we?␀␀␀␀ˇˇHere they are.  I think that's all of them.␀␀␀ˇˇI tell you he's a drunk.␀␀ˇˇYou!  With the bottle!␀␀␀␀ˇˇBut we must think of the children.␀␀␀␀ˇˇI don't like intruding in the private lives of my staff.␀␀ˇˇWhat's what?␀␀ˇˇGalloway is clearly a bad influence... just look at this young man.␀␀␀ˇˇYes Miss, I try my best.␀␀ˇˇPlease, take this.␀␀␀␀ˇˇYou are quite useful aren't you?␀␀ˇˇGet that kid!␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇThose bottles are around here somewhere.␀␀ˇˇI don't believe you're old enough for that.␀␀␀ˇˇThese are very serious allegations Mr. Hattrick␀␀␀ˇˇYou better not have led me on a wild goose chase Hattrick.␀␀␀␀ˇˇThat child had a bottle!␀␀ˇˇriverrun, past Eve and Adam's, from swerve of shore to bend of bay...uhm... yesh.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇUnderage drinking?  Oh you're in big trouble now.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇHey, stop right there.␀␀␀␀ˇˇJimmy, you're the only one I can count on to do this.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇThat is completely unacceptable... if what you're saying is true.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇGalloway's been recruiting students I see.  Well, we've got him now.␀␀ˇˇYou've earned the Camera.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇWhat have we here, Hopkins?␀␀␀ˇˇJust imagine!  Drinking in his class room.␀␀␀␀ˇˇI don't smell anything.  Come on.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇWhat's that?␀␀ˇˇ... maybe I should join the army... wouldn't be any worse than thish dump...␀␀ˇˇMy patience is wearing thin.␀␀ˇˇ... you know where you can shtick it Hattrick? I'll tell you where you can shtick it...␀␀␀ˇˇA drunk?  I'm not surprised.␀␀ˇˇThanks Jimmy.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇMoby you bastard! Where are you you big white tub of whale blubber?␀␀␀ˇˇThey are here somewhere.  He's thinks he's clever, but not clever enough.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇYou're welcome Ms.␀␀␀␀ˇˇI wish he would just quit drinking. I really do.␀␀ˇˇWe are getting nowhere, Mr. Hattrick.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇFind the bottle in the cafeteria.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇFind the bottle in the bathroom.␀␀ˇˇFind the bottle in the trophy case.␀␀␀ˇˇYou attacked Ms. Philips.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇThe school closed.␀␀␀␀ˇˇFind Galloway's hidden bottles.␀␀␀ˇˇTake the bottles to Ms. Philips.␀␀ˇˇI got you, you alcoholic miscreant.␀␀␀ˇˇOooh... Dr. Crabblesnitch is gonna love this.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇGet over here!␀␀␀␀ˇˇWhat's that you have there?␀␀␀ˇˇOur young friend here has been helping Mr. Galloway.␀␀ˇˇHe's trying to hide the evidence!␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇProbably not Ms.  This is the last one by the way.␀␀␀␀ˇˇ...brings us by a commodius vicus of recirculation back to Howth Castle and Environs... I think␀␀␀ˇˇAnd WHY do you have booze?␀␀␀␀ˇˇI'm sure he's around here somewhere.␀␀ˇˇAlcohol!  Where did you get this?␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇHmmmm... there's something fishy here.␀␀␀␀ˇˇI'd offer you a sip... but it's probably not a good idea.␀␀␀␀␀ˇˇThe best laid plans of mice and men gang aft awgly... eshpecially at Bullworth.␀␀␀≤é␀␀␀␀o"␀A␀␀␀qc␀u␀␀␀ÓÊ0␀≠␀␀␀ñº